cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite these maps, data or scripts as below."
title: "Mars Global Mosaic: Mapping Lava Flows, Fluvial Channels, and Impact Craters in Visible and Infrared"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Edwards
    given-names: Logan M
    affiliation: "Florida Institute of Technology"
abstract: >-
  An ArcGIS Pro project that co-registers Viking MDIM 2.1 colour, THEMIS day and night
  thermal infrared and the HRSC/MOLA blended elevation model of Mars on one ±60° grid and
  maps landforms over it in seven classes. A U-Net trained on a rule-made third label set
  leads, scored at 87.6% on held-out 15° blocks, beside a support vector machine on the
  same labels; four-class maps, crater and channel candidates checked against published
  catalogues, and tests of how much the thermal infrared adds are included. The release
  holds the maps, the trained models and the vector layers; the repository holds every
  script and the record each number is checked against. Coursework for OCN 4704 Remote
  Sensing, Fall 2026.
repository-code: "https://github.com/loggger101/Mars_Terrestrial_GlobalMosaic_GIS-Data"
